Short:        Settle The World Map Editor
Kurz:         Settle The World Map Editor
Uploader:     eliot@exdev.de (Andre Geisler)
Author:       eliot@exdev.de (Andre Geisler)
Type:         game/edit
Requires:     dev/misc/c2plib.lha
Version:      0.1.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1.4; ppc-morphos
Distribution: Aminet
URL:          https://github.com/eliot-exdev/stw-map-editor

Simple map editor for the Amiga strategy game Settle The World
(see: https://theotheoderich.itch.io/settle-the-world).

# Requirements

* MorphOs:
  Any MorphOs system should work.
  Tested it on a Mac Mini G4 Silent Upgrade with MorphOs 3.19.
  You will need a 640x480x8 screen mode.
* AmigaOs:
  Tested on: Amiga 4000T, 060, Cybervision 64/3D, Aos 3.2.3
             Amiga 1200, 060, AGA, Aos 3.2.3.
  AGA requires c2p.library from aminet, see:
  https://aminet.net/dev/misc/c2plib.lha

# Usage

There are three different Amiga executables.
Depending on your system, choose one of them:

- stw_map_editor_aos_060:
  For Amiga with 68060 cpu and graphics card.
  Resolution will be SVGA (640x480x8).
- stw_map_editor_aos_060_c2p
  For Amiga with 68060 cpu and AGA.
  Resolution will be PAL (320x256x8).
- stw_map_editor_aos_030_fpu_c2p
  For Amiga with 68030 cpu with fpu and AGA.
  Resolution will be PAL (320x256x8).

## Program arguments

stw_map_editor [ARGUMENTS]...
arguments:
-h, --help              print help message and exit
-v, --version           print version and exit
-m --map <path to map>  load map in path

Call the executable with the path to an existing map
which you want to modify.
Example:
  stw_map_editor_aos_060 -m maps/001.map

## Main screen

The main screen is split into 3 different areas:
- status bar on the top
- tile view on the right
- map view in the center

---------------------------------------------------------------
| Status bar                                      | Tile view |
|-------------------------------------------------|           |
|                                                 |           |
|                                                 |           |
| Map view                                        |           |
|                                                 |           |
|                                                 |           |
|                                                 |           |
|                                                 |           |
|                                                 |           |
|                                                 |           |
---------------------------------------------------------------

### The status bar
The status bar is on the top and shows the current selected tile, x and y
coordinates, variance button, save button and quit button.

Selected tile will change if you select another tile on tile view.
The x and y coordinates show your current position under the mouse pointer
in the map view. To shuffle all tile variants on the map,
you can press the variance button.
This operation will take some time depending on your cpu performance.
To save your current map, press the save button. Your given map file won't
overwritten. Instead a new file with suffix ".mod" will be created.
You can leave the editor by pressing the quit button or hit "ESC" key.

## The tile view

Here you can select you map tile which you want to place on map view.
For each tile there are three different variants.
Use the scroll bar on the right, to scroll up down to see all available tiles.

## The map view

Show your current map. You can look around by holding down the right mouse
button and move your mouse.
To place the current selected tile on map, press the left mouse button.

